# Eduxa Design System - CSS Guide

Complete CSS documentation for the Eduxa Design System, including design tokens, utility classes, and component styling patterns.

## Table of Contents

1. [Design Tokens](#design-tokens)
2. [CSS Custom Properties](#css-custom-properties)
3. [Utility Classes](#utility-classes)
4. [Component Styling](#component-styling)
5. [Dark Mode](#dark-mode)
6. [Responsive Design](#responsive-design)
7. [Best Practices](#best-practices)

---

## Design Tokens

Design tokens are the visual design atoms of the design system. They're stored as SCSS variables and exported as CSS custom properties for runtime customization.

### Color System

#### Brand Colors

```scss
// Primary (Indigo)
$eduxa-primary: #6366f1;        // Main brand color
$eduxa-primary-light: #818cf8;  // Lighter variant
$eduxa-primary-dark: #4f46e5;   // Darker variant

// Secondary (Sky)
$eduxa-secondary: #0ea5e9;
$eduxa-secondary-light: #38bdf8;
$eduxa-secondary-dark: #0284c7;
```

#### Semantic Colors

```scss
// Success (Emerald)
$eduxa-success: #10b981;
$eduxa-success-light: #34d399;
$eduxa-success-dark: #059669;

// Warning (Amber)
$eduxa-warning: #f59e0b;
$eduxa-warning-light: #fbbf24;
$eduxa-warning-dark: #d97706;

// Danger (Red)
$eduxa-danger: #ef4444;
$eduxa-danger-light: #f87171;
$eduxa-danger-dark: #dc2626;

// Info (Blue)
$eduxa-info: #3b82f6;
$eduxa-info-light: #60a5fa;
$eduxa-info-dark: #2563eb;
```

#### Neutral Colors (Gray Scale)

```scss
$eduxa-gray-50: #f9fafb;
$eduxa-gray-100: #f3f4f6;
$eduxa-gray-200: #e5e7eb;
$eduxa-gray-300: #d1d5db;
$eduxa-gray-400: #9ca3af;
$eduxa-gray-500: #6b7280;
$eduxa-gray-600: #4b5563;
$eduxa-gray-700: #374151;
$eduxa-gray-800: #1f2937;
$eduxa-gray-900: #111827;
```

#### Dark Mode Colors

```scss
$eduxa-dark-surface: #0f172a;         // Main dark background
$eduxa-dark-surface-light: #1e293b;  // Secondary dark background
$eduxa-dark-border: #334155;          // Dark borders
$eduxa-dark-text: #f1f5f9;            // Primary dark text
$eduxa-dark-text-secondary: #94a3b8; // Secondary dark text
```

### Typography

#### Font Family

```scss
$eduxa-font-family: 'Inter', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;
```

#### Font Sizes

```scss
$eduxa-font-size-xs: 0.75rem;   // 12px
$eduxa-font-size-sm: 0.875rem;  // 14px
$eduxa-font-size-base: 1rem;    // 16px
$eduxa-font-size-lg: 1.125rem;  // 18px
$eduxa-font-size-xl: 1.25rem;   // 20px
$eduxa-font-size-2xl: 1.5rem;   // 24px
$eduxa-font-size-3xl: 1.875rem; // 30px
$eduxa-font-size-4xl: 2.25rem;  // 36px
```

#### Font Weights

```scss
$eduxa-font-weight-light: 300;
$eduxa-font-weight-normal: 400;
$eduxa-font-weight-medium: 500;
$eduxa-font-weight-semibold: 600;
$eduxa-font-weight-bold: 700;
```

#### Line Heights

```scss
$eduxa-line-height-tight: 1.25;
$eduxa-line-height-normal: 1.5;
$eduxa-line-height-relaxed: 1.75;
```

### Spacing Scale

The spacing scale follows a 4px base unit system:

```scss
$eduxa-spacing-0: 0;        // 0px
$eduxa-spacing-1: 0.25rem;  // 4px
$eduxa-spacing-2: 0.5rem;   // 8px
$eduxa-spacing-3: 0.75rem;  // 12px
$eduxa-spacing-4: 1rem;     // 16px
$eduxa-spacing-5: 1.25rem;  // 20px
$eduxa-spacing-6: 1.5rem;   // 24px
$eduxa-spacing-8: 2rem;     // 32px
$eduxa-spacing-10: 2.5rem;  // 40px
$eduxa-spacing-12: 3rem;    // 48px
$eduxa-spacing-16: 4rem;    // 64px
```

### Border Radius

```scss
$eduxa-radius-none: 0;       // No radius
$eduxa-radius-sm: 0.125rem;  // 2px
$eduxa-radius-md: 0.375rem;  // 6px
$eduxa-radius-lg: 0.5rem;    // 8px
$eduxa-radius-xl: 0.75rem;   // 12px
$eduxa-radius-2xl: 1rem;     // 16px
$eduxa-radius-full: 9999px;  // Fully rounded
```

### Shadows

```scss
$eduxa-shadow-sm: 0 1px 2px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
$eduxa-shadow-md: 0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1), 0 2px 4px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
$eduxa-shadow-lg: 0 10px 15px -3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1), 0 4px 6px -2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
$eduxa-shadow-xl: 0 20px 25px -5px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1), 0 10px 10px -5px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.04);
```

### Transitions

```scss
$eduxa-transition-fast: 150ms;
$eduxa-transition-base: 200ms;
$eduxa-transition-slow: 300ms;
$eduxa-transition-easing: cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);
```

### Z-Index Scale

```scss
$eduxa-z-dropdown: 1000;
$eduxa-z-sticky: 1020;
$eduxa-z-fixed: 1030;
$eduxa-z-modal-backdrop: 1040;
$eduxa-z-modal: 1050;
$eduxa-z-popover: 1060;
$eduxa-z-tooltip: 1070;
```

---

## CSS Custom Properties

All design tokens are exported as CSS custom properties for runtime customization and usage in inline styles or JavaScript.

### Usage in CSS

```css
.my-component {
  background-color: var(--eduxa-primary);
  padding: var(--eduxa-spacing-4);
  border-radius: var(--eduxa-radius-lg);
  transition: all var(--eduxa-transition-base) var(--eduxa-transition-easing);
}
```

### Usage in Inline Styles

```vue
<template>
  <div :style="{
    backgroundColor: 'var(--eduxa-primary)',
    padding: 'var(--eduxa-spacing-4)',
    borderRadius: 'var(--eduxa-radius-lg)'
  }">
    Content
  </div>
</template>
```

### Runtime Customization

You can override CSS custom properties at runtime for dynamic theming:

```javascript
// Change primary color dynamically
document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--eduxa-primary', '#ff6b6b');

// Enable dark mode
document.documentElement.classList.add('dark-mode');
```

---

## Utility Classes

Utility classes provide single-purpose styling helpers for rapid development.

### Spacing Utilities

#### Margin

```html
<!-- All sides -->
