## Dark Mode

Dark mode is supported through CSS custom properties and class-based switching.

### Enabling Dark Mode

Add the `dark-mode` class to the root element:

```html
<html class="dark-mode">
```

Or toggle it dynamically:

```javascript
document.documentElement.classList.toggle('dark-mode');
```

### Dark Mode Overrides

The design system automatically applies dark mode styles when the `dark-mode` class is present:

```css
.dark-mode {
  background-color: var(--eduxa-dark-surface);
  color: var(--eduxa-dark-text);
}

.dark-mode .eduxa-card {
  background-color: var(--eduxa-dark-surface-light);
  border-color: var(--eduxa-dark-border);
}

.dark-mode .eduxa-input {
  background-color: var(--eduxa-dark-surface-light);
  border-color: var(--eduxa-dark-border);
  color: var(--eduxa-dark-text);
}

.dark-mode .eduxa-table th {
  background-color: var(--eduxa-dark-surface-light);
  color: var(--eduxa-dark-text);
}

.dark-mode .eduxa-table td {
  color: var(--eduxa-dark-text);
  border-color: var(--eduxa-dark-border);
}
```

### Custom Dark Mode Colors

You can customize dark mode colors by overriding CSS custom properties:

```css
.dark-mode {
  --eduxa-dark-surface: #0f172a;
  --eduxa-dark-surface-light: #1e293b;
  --eduxa-dark-border: #334155;
  --eduxa-dark-text: #f1f5f9;
  --eduxa-dark-text-secondary: #94a3b8;
}
```

