## Best Practices

### 1. Use Design Tokens

Always use design tokens instead of hardcoding values:

```css
/* ❌ Bad */
.my-component {
  padding: 16px;
  border-radius: 8px;
  background-color: #6366f1;
}

/* ✅ Good */
.my-component {
  padding: var(--eduxa-spacing-4);
  border-radius: var(--eduxa-radius-lg);
  background-color: var(--eduxa-primary);
}
```

### 2. Use Utility Classes for Simple Styles

For simple styling needs, use utility classes:

```html
<!-- ❌ Bad -->
<div class="my-component" style="padding: 16px; margin: 8px;">
  Content
</div>

<!-- ✅ Good -->
<div class="p-4 m-2">
  Content
</div>
```

### 3. Use Components for Complex UI

For complex UI patterns, use the provided components:

```vue
<!-- ❌ Bad -->
<div class="custom-card">
  <div class="custom-card-header">Title</div>
  <div class="custom-card-body">Content</div>
</div>

<!-- ✅ Good -->
<Card>
  <template #header>
    <h2>Title</h2>
  </template>
  <p>Content</p>
</Card>
```

### 4. Respect Spacing Scale

Stick to the spacing scale for consistency:

```css
/* ❌ Bad */
.my-component {
  padding: 13px;
  margin: 7px;
}

/* ✅ Good */
.my-component {
  padding: var(--eduxa-spacing-3);  /* 12px */
  margin: var(--eduxa-spacing-2);   /* 8px */
}
```

### 5. Use Semantic Colors

Use semantic colors for their intended purpose:

```css
/* ❌ Bad */
.error-message {
  color: var(--eduxa-primary);
}

/* ✅ Good */
.error-message {
  color: var(--eduxa-danger);
}
```

### 6. Add Transitions for Interactive Elements

Always add transitions for hover states and interactive elements:

```css
/* ❌ Bad */
.button {
  background-color: var(--eduxa-primary);
}

.button:hover {
  background-color: var(--eduxa-primary-dark);
}

/* ✅ Good */
.button {
  background-color: var(--eduxa-primary);
  transition: background-color var(--eduxa-transition-fast);
}

.button:hover {
  background-color: var(--eduxa-primary-dark);
}
```

### 7. Test Dark Mode

Always test your designs in both light and dark modes:

```css
/* ❌ Bad - only light mode */
.my-component {
  background-color: white;
  color: var(--eduxa-gray-900);
}

/* ✅ Good - both modes */
.my-component {
  background-color: white;
  color: var(--eduxa-gray-900);
}

.dark-mode .my-component {
  background-color: var(--eduxa-dark-surface-light);
  color: var(--eduxa-dark-text);
}
```

### 8. Use Appropriate Border Radius

Use border radius that matches the component's purpose:

```css
/* ❌ Bad - inconsistent */
.button {
  border-radius: 4px;
}

.card {
  border-radius: 2px;
}

/* ✅ Good - consistent */
.button {
  border-radius: var(--eduxa-radius-lg);
}

.card {
  border-radius: var(--eduxa-radius-xl);
}
```

### 9. Consider Accessibility

Ensure sufficient color contrast and use semantic HTML:

```html
<!-- ❌ Bad - poor contrast -->
<div style="color: #ccc; background-color: #666;">
  Hard to read text
</div>

<!-- ✅ Good - accessible contrast -->
<div style="color: var(--eduxa-gray-900); background-color: white;">
  Easy to read text
</div>
```

### 10. Organize Your CSS

Keep your CSS organized and modular:

```css
/* ❌ Bad - everything in one place */
.my-component {
  /* 50 lines of mixed styles */
}

/* ✅ Good - organized */
.my-component {
  /* Layout */
  display: flex;
  gap: var(--eduxa-spacing-4);

  /* Typography */
  font-size: var(--eduxa-font-size-base);
  color: var(--eduxa-gray-900);

  /* Spacing */
  padding: var(--eduxa-spacing-4);

  /* Borders */
  border: 1px solid var(--eduxa-gray-200);
  border-radius: var(--eduxa-radius-lg);

  /* Transitions */
  transition: all var(--eduxa-transition-base);
}
```

